### O017-D2

O017-D2, item_version 1, full_capability_check. **Prompt:** A random walk with drift satisfies $x_t=a+x_{t-1}+\varepsilon_t$, with $a=0.2$, i.i.d. zero-mean innovations of variance 2 independent of $x_0$, $E[x_0]=-2$ and $\operatorname{Var}(x_0)=5$. Derive the accumulated representation, mean/variance at $t=9$, and the 5-period forecast from current level 11. Derive first differences and classify levels/differences in the course’s $I(1)/I(0)$ framing. Compare removing a deterministic trend from $z_t=b_0+b_1t+v_t$ with removing drift from this random walk. Explain why sample lag-one correlation, a fitted trend, or high regression fit cannot establish stationarity, a unit root, causality or valid usual inference. State the scope of the lecture’s DF/ADF pointers.

**Complete solution and essential rubric:** Iteration yields $x_t=x_0+at+\sum_{j=1}^t\varepsilon_j$, so $E[x_t]=E[x_0]+at=-0.20000000$ and $\operatorname{Var}(x_t)=\operatorname{Var}(x_0)+t\sigma_\varepsilon^2=23.00000000$. Independent random initialization requires retaining its variance/expectation; dropping the variance is valid only if fixed. The forecast is $E[x_{t+h}\mid x_t]=x_t+ah=12.00000000$; a shock’s level coefficient remains one. $\Delta x_t=a+\varepsilon_t$ has mean 0.2, variance 2, and is i.i.d. $I(0)$ here; levels are $I(1)$ and nonstationary because variance grows. General $I(1)$ differences can retain weak dependence and need not be i.i.d. Subtracting $at$ leaves accumulated shocks, whereas removing the correct deterministic trend from the trend-stationary $z_t$ exposes stationary weakly dependent $v_t$. Differencing changes interpretation from level to change and does not automatically fix endogeneity/inference. Large lag-one correlation is a persistence diagnostic, not proof of an exact unit root; detrending is not a universal unit-root remedy. Unrelated persistent levels can produce misleading high fit/usual significance, without proving every regression involving an $I(1)$ variable is spurious. DF/ADF are named leads only: their regressions, critical values and procedures are outside this prepared scope. All requested calculations, derivations and qualifications are essential; the component map above applies to every full form.

